ctually i  thought there was this eeriness to it  about trying to figure out what's going  on interesting stuff happening with  these adult film stars and kind of  seeing where it was going to head and he  was doing a good job at like sprinkling  the old couple in and you're like okay  this is weird what is happening and it  felt you know at points maybe not super  original but other points very original  and i think where that originality comes  in is having it be this old couple these  villains in the with pearl and i like  that pearl had a good motivation you  know that she missed being you know this  beautiful woman being attractive she  missed having just sex on the regular  and now she's seeing it in maxine and i  really love the scene where she looks  into the shed and sees maxine having sex  and doing this and doing her thing and  you know she's envy of that right it's  it's a good motivation for the villain  and i like how they tied it around with  her when she danced when she did her  first kill in this movie and that they  brought that up they did a lot of good  things that they planted and paid off  later perfect example that is even with  the alligator right i loved loved the  shot that was overhead of maxine's  swimming and the alligators following  her  that was memorable to me and to get the  payoff then  of the alligator  eating britney snow's characters head  off my favorite kill of the film that  was incredible i do wish there was  better kills though because in the  slasher the kills really gotta land  i thought most of them were good but  some were a little lazy especially the  death of kid cuddy's character so that  was a little disappointing in my other  disappointments of the film is i did  feel like after the first 30 40 minutes  it slowed down a little too much until  we got to the final act or picked up  again so i think it had a little bit of  pacing issues the movie was about an  hour 45 minutes i actually think he  could have chopped out some of that  middle and made an hour and 30 it might  have felt tighter and more exciting uh  for where it got a little too slow for  my taste but again i thought the music  was really good and one of the hardest  laughs i've actually didn't expect in a  film like this was when we saw that jen  ortega's character is this  catholic good girl who's set up as this  prude character but then she starts  opening up she wants to be in the film  and that she's wearing the underwear  that says you know sunday on it i  thought that was hysterical that was one  of the hardest laughs i had in a while  so props for that and  there was you know such inspiration from  texas chainsaw massacre here and i felt  that and it wasn't as good as texas  chainsaw massacre but that's you know  high standards but it did its good job  of like showing love for those type of  films but making its own different voice  to it again i think there it was so  close to being great i think this is a  good film  um i just felt like maybe i wish there  was something more here something more  that sticks with you that like in the  mind makes you feel hard which that  usually happens with a24 films or  something psychological horror about  this but i think it was kind of going  for that but didn't really land for me  and that aspect like i'm not thinking  about it after i think it's just a fun  time which yes it was meant to be but i  do think it was attempting to kind of  bring that in and it didn't actually  work as well as it should have so that's  where i was a little disappointed but  overall  i really enjoyed this film and it was a  surreal experience you know my mom  loved the movie which was awesome so  that was cool too to see you know that  that was like a twist for me so it's  doing something right you know and  i thought it was really good so i'm  actually going to give this one an 8.1  and i didn't even stay for the post  credits i didn't know there was one so i  watched on youtube so check 